  "body": {
    "id": "lem:parametric-moment-floor",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "There is a constant \\(c_{\\mathrm{par}}>0\\), depending only on \\(M_1\\) and \\(M_2\\), such that for every \\(T\\ge1\\) and every \\(C\\ge1\\),\n\\[\n R_T(t_0,\\zeta,C)\\ge c_{\\mathrm{par}}T^{-1}.\n\\]\nThe lower bound holds on a one-state binary-action subexperiment with \\(b=e\\) and independent scaled Rademacher rewards.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(T\\)",
      "\\(C\\)",
      "\\(M_1\\)",
      "\\(M_2\\)",
      "\\(R_T(t_0,\\zeta,C)\\)",
      "\\(t_0\\)",
      "\\(\\zeta\\)",
      "\\(b\\)",
      "\\(e\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:pomdp-kernel",
      "ass:sequential-ignorability",
      "ass:stationary-start",
      "ass:bounded-reward",
      "ass:policy-overlap",
      "ass:uniform-contraction",
      "ass:latent-stationary-overlap",
      "def:model-class",
      "def:target-value",
      "def:minimax-risk",
      "def:tagged-decision-rules",
      "lem:two-point-testing-overlap"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Take singleton observed and hidden state spaces, \\(\\mathcal A=\\{0,1\\}\\), and \\(b=e=(1/2,1/2)\\).  The state never moves.  Its contraction coefficient is zero, its two stationary laws coincide, and both overlap assumptions hold for every \\(t_0>0\\), \\(\\zeta>0\\), and \\(C\\ge1\\).  Put \\(\\eta_T:=1/(4\\sqrt T)\\).  Under alternative \\(v\\in\\{-1,+1\\}\\), let the rewards be independent with values \\(\\pm\\gamma_0\\) and standardized mean \\(v\\eta_T\\).  Their conditional mean has magnitude \\(\\gamma_0\\eta_T\\le M_1\\), and their conditional second moment is \\(\\gamma_0^2\\le M_2\\), so both alternatives belong to the model class and have the same supplied design.  Their target values are \\(\\theta_v=v\\gamma_0\\eta_T\\).\n\nFor the present scaled Rademacher experiment, direct substitution into the two point masses and \\(\\log u\\le u-1\\) give\n\\[\n \\operatorname{KL}(P_+\\|P_-)\n \\le T\\frac{4\\eta_T^2}{1-\\eta_T^2}\\le\\frac4{15}.\n\\]\nApply \\(\\mathrm{lem{:}two\\text{-}point\\text{-}testing\\text{-}overlap}\\) with \\(a=\\gamma_0/(4\\sqrt T)\\).  Since the pair shares one design tag, every admissible tagged decision family restricts to an estimator in this two-point experiment.  Taking the supremum and then the infimum in \\(\\mathrm{def{:}minimax\\text{-}risk}\\) yields\n\\[\n R_T(t_0,\\zeta,C)\n \\ge\\frac{\\gamma_0^2e^{-4/15}}{64}\\,T^{-1}.\n\\]\nThis proves the result with \\(c_{\\mathrm{par}}=\\gamma_0^2e^{-4/15}/64>0\\).",
    "justification": "The parametric subexperiment supplies the unavoidable risk floor at equality and below the overlap elbow.",
    "gap": "A local hidden-state lower bound alone vanishes at equality and cannot establish the full uniform frontier.",
    "consumer": "It joins the equality endpoint to the hidden-state lower bound.",
